11929	{"artifactId":"HLD-c66d49bb81925886","entry":{"id":"review-99a42bd0cc1c8467006f6ef02785a444","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:01:40.205Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The accounting design covers the upstream mandatory activity-to-charged-artifact rules.","evidence":"DEF constraint k7 requires: “Reviews charge the reviewed LLD, task work charges TASK, and shared story validation/code review charges BUILD.” The stakeholder source additionally says CR references must not copy BUILD charges. HLD defines generic ownership validation and explicit bindings but never specifies these activity-to-owner rules or assigns their validation to a story. Correct root resolution alone does not enforce correct charged-artifact selection. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md, plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c1.txt, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md]","action":"Specify the mandatory attribution table, identify the story owning its validation, and distinguish validating supplied attribution in TU1 from automatic capture in TU2/TU3.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing artifact parent contracts do not constitute the proposed complete usage-root resolver.","evidence":"ArtifactIds.parentOf handles TASK/TASKS/DIAG → STORY and STORY → EPIC, returning undefined otherwise. Artifact.parent is optional; decodeArtifactHead preserves that optional reference. ArtifactStore.checkLinks checks the expected canonical parent only when parentOf supplies one. These contracts do not supply the proposed document/standalone reservation semantics. [files: src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/decode.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts]","action":"Retain the explicit evidence-backed usage-binding resolver.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing artifact journal and atomic writer do not establish the proposed Avro durability protocol.","evidence":"StagedOperation contains artifact-head bytes and a ChangeLogEntry. createFileJournal stages JSON through writeAtomic. That function performs mkdirSync, writeFileSync and renameSync, without file or directory fsync. The design correctly treats durable Avro blocks and checkpoints as additional work. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"Keep the new durability protocol independent of artifact-head journaling.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed service can reuse existing daemon content services and Avro conversion without treating them as an existing usage appender.","evidence":"lifecycleFor canonicalizes repository paths and shares store/service instances. avroConverter validates container framing, decodes bounded blocks and writes typed Parquet; duckdb-file maps converted Avro to read_parquet. package.json includes avsc. None of these inspected implementations provides the proposed append-intent/checkpoint service. Repository filename search found no usage-accounting implementation. The analyzer request returned no bundle before cancellation, so this assessment rests on direct source reads and search. [files: src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts, src/daemon/db/drivers/converters/avro.ts, src/daemon/db/drivers/duckdb-file.ts, package.json]","action":"Retain schema/converter qualification as build acceptance rather than claiming existing compatibility with the proposed record schema.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"At HLD granularity, the proposed contracts identify ownership and dependency direction sufficiently without requiring changes to existing provider callers.","evidence":"The inspected lifecycle registry supplies a per-repository composition point, while converter and DuckDB modules provide the stated query boundary. HLD assigns sc1–sc6 owners and consumers, keeps capture callers outside TU1, and explicitly delegates exact handler registration and files to LLDs. No existing usage API signature is being represented as already implemented. [files: src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts, src/daemon/db/drivers/duckdb-file.ts, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md]","action":"Carry exact registry/configuration/handler changes and consumer signatures into the corresponding LLD inventories.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The relationship and interaction documentation is adequate at the source level.","evidence":"The generated ER source specifies RootLedger-to-record and artifact-to-record cardinalities. HLD prose additionally specifies repository/root ownership, immutable physical membership, effective attribution, and source/destination transfer references. The sequence source orders durable intent, ledger fsync, checkpoint sync and receipt; component source places the pure domain beneath the daemon service. Snapshot and transfer ordering are supplied in prose. Together these cover the material relationships without requiring a UX mock. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/er-model.html, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/sequence-diagram.html, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/component-dependency.html]","action":"Optionally distinguish usage observations from non-billable controls in the ER edge label “chargedRecords”; the prose already makes that distinction.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The linked generated companions render correctly and remain visually consistent with the design.","evidence":"Read the Mermaid source embedded in all three generated HTML companions. Attempted to open the ER companion through browser automation, which returned “Browser is not available: iab”. No rendered diagram was inspected; layout, clipping and runtime Mermaid rendering remain unverified. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/er-model.html, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/sequence-diagram.html, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/component-dependency.html]","action":"Render and visually inspect all three existing companions; correct or regenerate any rendering defects.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design preserves existing artifact content and handles absent or incompatible usage data explicitly.","evidence":"decodeArtifactHead already supports missing envelope/lifecycle metadata through defaults. contentHash hashes only canonical description, body and citations. HLD introduces an external namespace, prohibits content mutation for usage, distinguishes legacy absence from zero, fixes each container to its header writer schema, and requires explicit migration with backup for incompatible changes. The inspected Avro converter reads its type from the header, consistent with that restriction. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/decode.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/daemon/db/drivers/converters/avro.ts, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md]","action":"Retain legacy-content and unsupported-schema preservation fixtures in implementation acceptance.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed story allocation respects the upstream foundation scope and existing storage boundaries.","evidence":"DEF excludes capture, controller reporting, hierarchy totals, board UI and replacement of generic artifact storage. HLD retains those exclusions and the s1 → s2 → s3 → s4 dependency order. Existing lifecycle services remain content owners; DuckDBInstance.create(':memory:') confirms the reused query engine is disposable rather than a second persistent store. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts, src/daemon/db/duckdb-pool.ts]","action":"Preserve these exclusions when downstream LLDs introduce concrete adapters.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The designed persistence and transfer failures are detectable and have conservative handling.","evidence":"Against DEF s2/ac2–ac5 and s3/ac6, HLD distinguishes committed-prefix corruption from uncommitted torn tails, requires matching intent for repair, makes missing checkpoint recovery-required, blocks writes on identity-index conflicts, and preserves the original charge until a validated transfer pair commits. Existing journal recovery also exposes head-change conflicts, but its weaker head protocol is explicitly not reused as proof of Avro durability. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts]","action":"Implement the stated phase fault injection and verify every failure preserves acknowledged history without requesting inference replay.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Every upstream acceptance criterion maps to a planned test.","evidence":"DEF enumerates 23 acceptance criteria across s1–s4. HLD names broad deterministic accounting fixtures, lifecycle tests, durability fault injection and scale/query qualification, but supplies no complete criterion-to-test mapping. In particular, s1/ac6 requires qualified evidence about native/external source capabilities; generic granularity types and reducer fixtures do not specify that qualification evidence or its test. The attribution cases required by k7 likewise have no explicit test mapping. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/HLD.md, plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c1.txt]","action":"Add a compact matrix mapping all 23 criteria to planned fixtures or qualification checks, owning story and expected assertion. Include source-capability qualification without requiring TU2/TU3 instrumentation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":9,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T08:01:40.205Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
