569	{"artifactId":"HLD-c66d49bb81925886","entry":{"id":"ed46e9b51d2741f992207186f5c9a28b","actor":{"id":"insrc:controller","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:07:53.236Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":3,"contentHash":"16e637e306c1a73a57223f8dbbf5dff1d7ab36d98b5bf0abac5077965f53402c"},"outcome":{"result":"revised","summary":"Address HLD review round 1 MEDs: explicit mandatory attribution rules owned by s1/sc2 and complete 23-criterion fixture/qualification mapping; no implementation or automatic capture claimed."},"addresses":"all"}}
9521	{"artifactId":"HLD-c66d49bb81925886","entry":{"id":"review-1b5b550a2da06a465930fe70b0acc7ef","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:08:38.063Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The HLD covers the upstream foundation requirements without including later capture, hierarchy or board implementation.","evidence":"Compared DEF functional requirements, constraints k1–k10 and all four story acceptance sets with the HLD. Identity/reconciliation, durable root storage, reservation, lifecycle preservation, transfer and daemon access are designed. DEF non-goals explicitly exclude provider instrumentation, host reporting and subtree totals; HLD retains those exclusions. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md]","action":"Preserve these exclusions in the Story LLDs.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing artifact identities and envelopes do not provide the complete proposed usage-root resolver.","evidence":"Read ArtifactIds parsing/shape rules and parentOf, plus Artifact and decodeArtifactHead. parentOf handles TASK/TASKS/DIAG → STORY and STORY → EPIC, with default undefined. Artifact.parent is optional; decoding validates and returns the reference without resolving accounting ownership. [files: src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/decode.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing artifact journaling does not establish the proposed durable Avro commit protocol.","evidence":"Read createFileJournal and writeAtomic. The journal serializes staged artifact-head operations. writeAtomic performs mkdirSync, writeFileSync and renameSync; it contains no file or directory fsync. The HLD correctly treats Avro framing, checkpoints and durable acknowledgement as new work. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing Avro converter and in-memory DuckDB engine are valid reuse foundations, with ledger-schema compatibility still requiring qualification.","evidence":"Read the Avro converter's header, block, row and conversion implementations, readerExpression, and getDuckDB. Avro is bounded and converted to Parquet; converted kinds use read_parquet. DuckDB is created with ':memory:' and attempts to disable extension autoinstall/autoload. package.json includes avsc ^5.7.9. None supplies a durable appender or proves the proposed schema's exact query representation. [files: src/daemon/db/drivers/converters/avro.ts, src/daemon/db/drivers/duckdb-file.ts, src/daemon/db/duckdb-pool.ts, package.json]","action":"Retain exact-counter and nested-schema qualification before enabling the service.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The HLD identifies suitable existing integration boundaries and separates proposed shared contracts from existing signatures.","evidence":"Read lifecycleFor and createRepoLifecycle: the daemon registry canonicalizes paths and caches repository content services assembled from store, history and lifecycle components. HLD sc1–sc6 explicitly describe proposed interfaces, assign owners/consumers, and defer exact handler registration and file layout to LLDs. Existing content journaling and identity APIs are preserved. [files: src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/repo-lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts]","action":"In LLDs, make the s2-to-s3 interface for ordered multi-root locking and transfer recovery explicit; the HLD sketches do not expose that mechanism.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The generated ER, sequence and component companions render consistently with the HLD.","evidence":"Read the embedded Mermaid sources in all three HTML companions. They describe root/record cardinalities, durable append ordering and dependency direction consistent with the principal prose. Rendering was attempted: the in-app browser was unavailable, and Chrome rejected the local file URL under its protocol policy. Layout, clipping and actual Mermaid execution were not verified. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/er-model.html, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/sequence-diagram.html, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/component-dependency.html]","action":"Render all three existing companions in an environment permitted to open them and inspect their visual consistency.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design preserves existing artifact storage while explicitly handling absent and unsupported usage histories.","evidence":"Read Artifact, decodeArtifactHead and contentHash. Existing envelopes contain no required usage field; legacy envelopes receive empty/default parts. contentHash hashes description, body and citations. The proposed separate namespace preserves those shapes, distinguishes missing/legacy/unsupported from zero, fixes each container's writer schema and requires an approved recoverable migration for incompatible changes. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/decode.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md]","action":"None; verify these planned guarantees with the specified legacy and byte-independence fixtures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Story ownership and dependency order preserve the DEF boundaries and document the new ownership relationships.","evidence":"DEF establishes s2 after s1, s3 after s2, and s4 after s2/s3. HLD preserves that order and assigns domain semantics to s1, persistence/bindings/snapshots to s2, lifecycle/transfer to s3 and daemon qualification to s4. Prose specifies repository-to-root and root-to-record cardinality, physical versus effective ownership, transfer direction and compatibility. Existing identity/content contracts remain intact. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md, src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts]","action":"None. The relationship prose is adequate without requiring additional diagrams; retain it alongside the companions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed durability and accounting failure paths have explicit detection and conservative outcomes.","evidence":"Compared DEF k3/k6/k9 and s2/s3/s4 failure criteria against the HLD protocol, accounting rules and result unions. The design distinguishes pre-ack failure, committed response loss, missing checkpoints, damaged committed bytes, unexplained suffixes, conflicting IDs, unsupported schemas and incomplete transfers. It blocks complete reporting or writes where proof is missing and prohibits inference replay as accounting repair. Existing writeAtomic is correctly not treated as sufficient durability evidence. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md, src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts]","action":"Carry every stated failure class into concrete LLD error contracts and fault injection.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream acceptance criterion maps to a planned qualification check.","evidence":"Enumerated the actual DEF acceptance sets: s1 has six, s2 five, s3 six and s4 six, totaling 23. The HLD matrix contains each identifier once and supplies fixtures and expected assertions, including capability evidence, crash boundaries, attribution refusals, lifecycle preservation, transfer recovery and converter qualification. It explicitly makes no claim that these tests already exist or pass. [files: docs/epics/retain-durable-artifact-token-usage-E20261026c66d49bb/DEF.md]","action":"Story LLDs must supply concrete test paths and preserve the complete mapping.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":10,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T08:08:38.063Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
